        <p>
          Dr Maryna Kuzmenko is a UK-based educator, author, and speaker on AI in agriculture. She teaches more than 3,000 students across 121 countries and writes the AI in Agriculture book series, beginning with The Precision Vineyard, a field guide to AI, sensors and robotics in viticulture. Her teaching returns to one problem: a measurement that matters is locked behind specialist equipment, so the people who need it never take it. With Petiole Pro that measurement was leaf area and the answer was a smartphone camera — tools now used by research organisations on six continents. With MooMore, which won the Innovate UK Women in Innovation Award 2026, it is inflammation in dairy cattle and the answer is a thermal sensor.
        </p>
