      <article class="bio-card">
        <h3>First-person bio</h3>
        <p>
          I teach AI in agriculture — to more than 3,000 students across 121 countries — and I write about it, most recently in The Precision Vineyard, a field guide for growers weighing up sensors and robotics. I also build the thing I teach: MooMore uses thermal imaging and on-device AI to catch lameness in dairy cows before anyone can see it, and it won the Innovate UK Women in Innovation Award in 2026. Before this I spent a decade on the crop side, building measurement tools now used by research organisations on six continents.
